---
import LegalPage from '../../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import { localeFromAstro, pathFor, useTranslations } from '../../i18n';

/**
 * English privacy policy.
 *
 * A translation for readers; the German version is the binding one, which the
 * page states up front.
 */
const locale = localeFromAstro(Astro.currentLocale);
const t = useTranslations(locale);
const { legal, host } = site;
const analyticsEnabled = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID);
---

<LegalPage
    page="privacy"
    title={t.meta.privacy.title}
    heading="Privacy Policy"
    description={t.meta.privacy.description}
    lastUpdated="Last updated: September 2026"
>
    <p>
        This is a translation for convenience. The
        <a href="/datenschutz/" hreflang="de" lang="de">German version</a> is the
        binding one.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <address>
        {legal.company}<br />
        {legal.street}<br />
        {legal.postalCode} {legal.city}, Germany<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </address>

    <h2>2. What this site does and does not do</h2>
    <p>
        This website sets no cookies of its own. Fonts and icons are served from
        our own domain, so opening a page contacts no third party. Nothing that
        is not strictly necessary loads until you agree to it.
    </p>
    <p>
        Your privacy choice is kept in your browser's local storage. It stays on
        your device and is never sent to us.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>This site is hosted by {host.name}, {host.address}.</p>
    <p>
        When you open a page, the web server processes technically necessary data:
        IP address, date and time, the page requested, the amount of data
        transferred, your browser, your operating system and the referring URL.
        This is needed to deliver the site and keep it stable and secure. The
        legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
    </p>
    <p>
        Netlify processes this data on our behalf under a data processing
        agreement (Art. 28 GDPR). Processing in the United States cannot be ruled
        out; it takes place under Art. 44 ff. GDPR on the basis of the standard
        contractual clauses Netlify uses.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Google Maps</h2>
    <p>
        We offer a Google Maps map on the venue page. The provider for users in
        the European Economic Area is Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House,
        Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>The map only loads after you ask for it.</strong> Until you press
        "Load map", there is no connection to Google. After that, data such as
        your IP address, browser and device information, the time of the request
        and technical usage data are sent to Google. If you are signed in to a
        Google account at the same time, Google may associate the use with your
        account.
    </p>
    <p>
        The legal basis is your consent under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR together with
        § 25(1) TDDDG.
    </p>

    {
        analyticsEnabled && (
            <>
                <h2>5. Google Analytics</h2>
                <p>
                    We use Google Analytics 4 (Google Ireland Limited) to see
                    which pages people visit. It loads{' '}
                    <strong>only after you agree</strong>. Without your consent
                    there is no measurement and no cookie is set.
                </p>
                <p>
                    After you agree, the following may be processed: a shortened
                    IP address, device and browser information, the pages you
                    open, how long you stay and the referring page. Google
                    Analytics 4 always shortens the IP address and never stores
                    it in full. Google signals and ad personalisation are off.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The legal basis is your consent under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR
                    together with § 25(1) TDDDG. You can withdraw it at any time
                    from the cookie settings in the footer.
                </p>
            </>
        )
    }

    <h2>{analyticsEnabled ? '6' : '5'}. Bookings through Eversports</h2>
    <p>
        We use Eversports (Eversport GmbH, Jakov-Lind-Straße 13/H/5th floor, 1020
        Vienna, Austria) to take and manage class bookings. Our site only links to
        Eversports; a connection is made when you follow one of those links.
    </p>
    <p>
        A booking may involve your name, email address, phone number, booking
        data, payment and invoice data. Where Eversports provides booking and
        participant management for us, it acts as our processor under Art. 28
        GDPR, and our own processing rests on Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR. Eversports' own
        platform features are covered by its own privacy information.
    </p>

    <h2>{analyticsEnabled ? '7' : '6'}. Urban Sports Club</h2>
    <p>
        Midnight Havana is a partner of Urban Sports GmbH, Novalisstraße 10, 10115
        Berlin. If you attend on a membership, we receive your name, membership
        number, check-in information and the class, date and time. The legal basis
        is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR.
    </p>

    <h2>{analyticsEnabled ? '8' : '7'}. Payments at the venue</h2>
    <p>
        Card payments are handled by SumUp (SumUp Limited, Block 8, Harcourt
        Centre, Charlotte Way, Dublin 2, D02 K580, Ireland). We never receive your
        full card details. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR, and Art. 6(1)(c)
        GDPR for the records we must keep. Paying cash involves no personal
        payment data.
    </p>

    <h2>{analyticsEnabled ? '9' : '8'}. Contacting us</h2>
    <p>
        If you write to us by email, on Instagram or on WhatsApp, we process what
        you send us in order to answer. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR for
        booking-related messages and Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR otherwise. We delete the
        data once your enquiry is dealt with and nothing obliges us to keep it.
    </p>

    <h2>{analyticsEnabled ? '10' : '9'}. WhatsApp community and Instagram</h2>
    <p>
        Joining our WhatsApp community is voluntary. The provider is WhatsApp
        Ireland Limited, Merrion Road, Dublin 4, Ireland. Your mobile number,
        profile name, messages and the time of your messages may be processed. The
        legal basis is your consent under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, and you can leave at
        any time.
    </p>
    <p>
        We run an Instagram profile (Meta Platforms Ireland Limited, Merrion Road,
        Dublin 4, Ireland). Our site only links to it; no connection to Meta is
        made until you follow the link.
    </p>

    <h2>{analyticsEnabled ? '11' : '10'}. Photos and video at events</h2>
    <p>
        Photos and video may be taken at our events and used to document them and
        to promote Midnight Havana. For overview and group shots we rely on Art.
        6(1)(f) GDPR together with §§ 22 and 23 of the German Art Copyright Act.
        For portraits of an individual we ask for consent under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you would rather not be photographed or filmed, tell the event team or
        the photographer. You may object under Art. 21 GDPR to processing based on
        Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
    </p>

    <h2>{analyticsEnabled ? '12' : '11'}. How long we keep data</h2>
    <p>
        We keep personal data only as long as it is needed for the purpose it was
        collected for, unless commercial or tax law requires us to keep it longer.
    </p>

    <h2>{analyticsEnabled ? '13' : '12'}. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
        You have the right of access (Art. 15 GDPR), rectification (Art. 16),
        erasure (Art. 17), restriction of processing (Art. 18) and data
        portability (Art. 20). Where we process data under Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, you
        have a right to object under Art. 21. You may withdraw any consent at any
        time with effect for the future.
    </p>

    <h2>{analyticsEnabled ? '14' : '13'}. Right to complain</h2>
    <p>
        Under Art. 77 GDPR you may complain to a supervisory authority. Ours is
        the Berlin Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information,
        Alt-Moabit 59–61, 10555 Berlin, phone +49 30 13889-0, email
        <a href="mailto:mailbox@datenschutz-berlin.de"
            >mailbox@datenschutz-berlin.de</a
        >.
    </p>

    <h2>{analyticsEnabled ? '15' : '14'}. Automated decision-making</h2>
    <p>
        We do not use automated decision-making or profiling within the meaning of
        Art. 22 GDPR.
    </p>

    <hr />
    <p>
        See also our <a href={pathFor('terms', locale)}>terms and conditions</a> and
        our <a href={pathFor('imprint', locale)}>imprint</a>.
    </p>
</LegalPage>
